'''Michael Paul Mazzei''' (born May 30, 1965) is an American politician. A [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]], he was a member of the [[Oklahoma Senate]] from 2004 to 2016 and was the Oklahoma Secretary of Budget in 2019 and 2020.

Mazzei is the Republican nominee for Governor of Oklahoma in the [[2026 Oklahoma gubernatorial election|2026 election]].

==Early life, family, and education==
Mazzei was born on May 30, 1965.<ref name="birthday">{{cite web|title=Mazzei, Drummond advance to runoff election for Oklahoma governor|url= https://www.kosu.org/2026-oklahoma-governor-primary-election-results|website=kosu.org|publisher=[[KOSU]]|access-date=June 22, 2026|language=en}}</ref> He earned a [[Bachelor of Arts]] from [[George Mason University]] and a [[Master of Science]] from the [[Kaplan, Inc.|College for Financial Planning]]. He founded The Financial Coach Inc.<ref name="Ballotpedia">{{cite web |title=Mike Mazzei |url=https://ballotpedia.org/Mike_Mazzei |website=ballotpedia.org |publisher=[[Ballotpedia]] |access-date=April 1, 2025 |language=en}}</ref> He is the chairman and CEO of Trinity Strategic Wealth, a wealth and investment management firm based in [[Tulsa, Oklahoma]].<ref name="hoberock">{{cite web |title= Mazzei wants to bring financial skills to Oklahoma Governor’s Office |url= https://oklahomavoice.com/2026/06/03/mazzei-wants-to-bring-financial-skills-to-governors-office/ |website= oklahomavoice.com |access-date=June 22, 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="trinity">{{cite web |title= Mike Mazzei, CFP®, MPAS®: Chairman & CEO |url= https://www.trinitystrategicwealth.com/team-directory/mike-mazzei |website= trinitystrategicwealth.com |access-date=June 22, 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="fullname">{{cite web |title= MICHAEL PAUL MAZZEI — CRD#: 2023546 |url= https://adviserinfo.sec.gov/individual/summary/2023546 |website=adviserinfo.sec.gov |access-date=June 22, 2026 |language=en}}</ref>

He and his wife reside in Tulsa, and have five adult children. He is a member of Asbury Church.<ref name="Senate Bio">{{cite web |title=Senator Mike Mazzei - District 25 |url=http://www.oksenate.gov/Senators/biographies/mazzei_bio.html |website=oksenate.gov |publisher=[[Oklahoma Senate]] |access-date=April 1, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121008193231/http://www.oksenate.gov/Senators/biographies/mazzei_bio.html |archive-date=October 8, 2012}}</ref>

==Oklahoma Senate==
Mazzei was elected to the [[Oklahoma Senate]] by a majority in a five-person [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] primary in 2004.<ref name="2004 primary results" /> The [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic Party]] did not field a candidate and no independent or third-party candidate filed for the general election.{{cn|date=April 2025}} In 2007, he was appointed the assistant floor leader of the senate.<ref name="Senate Bio" />

Mazzei faced no opposition in his 2008 election bid. In 2012, he faced a challenge in the Republican Primary election. He defeated Ronda Vuillemont-Smith to secure re-election. He was term limited in 2016 and was succeeded in office by [[Joe Newhouse]].<ref name="Ballotpedia" />

==Stitt administration and later career==
In 2019 and 2020, Mazzei served as Oklahoma Secretary of Budget, under Governor Kevin Stitt.<ref name="2021 withdraw" /> In August 2021, Mazzei announced a campaign for [[Oklahoma State Treasurer]], but dropped out of the race the following month.<ref>{{cite news |title=Term-Limited Oklahoma Senator To Seek Open Treasurer Seat |url=https://www.publicradiotulsa.org/local-regional/2021-08-18/term-limited-oklahoma-senator-to-seek-open-treasurer-seat |access-date=April 1, 2025 |work=[[Public Radio Tulsa]] |agency=[[Associated Press]] |date=August 18, 2021 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="2021 withdraw">{{cite news |last1=Krehbiel |first1=Randy |title=Mike Mazzei drops out of treasurer race |url=https://tulsaworld.com/news/local/mike-mazzei-drops-out-of-treasurer-race/article_562dcbe0-1c93-11ec-a020-331dfbb7eddd.html |access-date=April 1, 2025 |work=[[Tulsa World]] |date=September 26, 2021 |language=en}}</ref>

In March 2025, Mazzei announced his candidacy for [[governor of Oklahoma]] in [[2026 Oklahoma gubernatorial election|2026]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hans |first1=Christian |title=Oklahoma Governor race: Former State Sen. Mike Mazzei announces candidacy |url=https://www.newson6.com/story/67ea7ca61e03566cb076c088/oklahoma-governor-race-mike-mazzei |access-date=April 1, 2025 |work=[[KOTV-DT]] |date=March 31, 2025}}</ref> He is the Republican candidate in the upcoming election.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gladden |first=Alex |title=Attention grows on Oklahoma governor's race between Mazzei, Munson |url=https://www.oklahoman.com/story/news/politics/2026/10/19/oklahoma-governors-race-mike-mazzei-cyndi-munson-final-weeks/92282222007/ |access-date=2026-10-20 |website=The Oklahoman |language=en-US}}</ref>

